        ]
      },
      "worked": "The original total is $4\\times\\left(-5\\frac{1}{3}\\right)=-\\frac{64}{3}$. The new total is $5\\times6\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{100}{3}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Fifth number}&=\\frac{100}{3}-\\left(-\\frac{64}{3}\\right)\\\\\\text{Fifth number}&=\\frac{164}{3}\\\\\\text{Fifth number}&=54\\frac{2}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
